# Next.js App Router Structure

## Route Organization

### Root Layout (`apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx`)
- **Purpose**: Global layout with `<html>` and `<body>` tags
- **Imports**: `globals.css`, fonts, AuthProvider
- **Applies to**: ALL routes in the application

### Route Groups
- `(public-sites)` - Group for public site routes
- `(admin)` - Group for admin routes (if exists)

### Nested Layouts
- `apps/web/src/app/(public-sites)/[site]/layout.tsx` - Site-specific layout
- **Important**: Must inherit from root layout, NOT create new HTML structure
- **Use**: `<>` (Fragment) instead of `<div>` to avoid duplicate HTML structure

## Route Structure

```
apps/web/src/app/
├── layout.tsx                    # Root layout (HTML, body, globals.css)
├── page.tsx                      # Home page (/)
├── login/
│   └── page.tsx                  # Login page (/login)
├── (public-sites)/              # Route group
│   └── [site]/                   # Dynamic site parameter
│       ├── layout.tsx            # Site layout (inherits from root)
│       ├── page.tsx              # Site home page (/[site])
│       ├── products/
│       │   └── page.tsx          # Products page (/[site]/products)
│       └── [...slug]/
│           └── page.tsx          # Dynamic content pages
└── admin/                        # Admin routes
    └── page.tsx                  # Admin dashboard (/admin)
```

## Key Rules

1. **Root Layout**: Only one layout with `<html>` and `<body>`
2. **Nested Layouts**: Use fragments `<>` to inherit from parent
3. **Global Styles**: Import `globals.css` only in root layout
4. **Route Groups**: Use `()` for organization without affecting URL structure
5. **Dynamic Routes**: Use `[]` for dynamic parameters

## Common Issues

- **Missing Styles**: Nested layout creating new HTML structure instead of inheriting
- **Duplicate HTML**: Using `<div>` instead of `<>` in nested layouts
- **Missing globals.css**: Not importing in root layout
